# Cursor tool mapping

When this session uses a **distinct Cursor product capability** in a meaningful way
(Plan mode, Bugbot, Security Review, MCP, rules, canvas, skills, Cloud Agents,
subagents, etc.), append a row to [`docs/cursor-tool-mapping.md`](docs/cursor-tool-mapping.md):

- when (date or stream)
- capability name as Cursor ships it
- what we actually did
- how to use / demo it (one sentence)

Do not add rows for ordinary Agent edits, greps, or commits. The mapping is evidence
of tools we used, not a changelog or a feature brochure. Prefer updating that file
over starting a new chat or subagent just to “remember” capabilities — subagents
do not persist.
